      "updated": 1791535415836,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "NOTES:\n\n- Neighbouring threads = neighbouring x.\n\n- Goal: neighbouring threads read neighbouring memory, so the reads combine.\n\n- Look at the linearizing formula: which one (row or col) is the \"+1\" term?\nrow-major: col (row * width + col)\ncol-major: row (col * height + row)\n\n- Put x into THAT one.\n\n- Both wirings give the correct answer. Only the speed changes.\n\n- Our matrices are row major, so x goes into col (the usual convention).\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "NOTES:\n\n- Neighbouring threads = neighbouring x.\n\n- Goal: neighbouring threads read neighbouring memory, so the reads combine.\n\n- Look at the linearizing formula: which one (row or col) is the \"+1\" term?\nrow-major: col (row * width + col)\ncol-major: row (col * height + row)\n\n- Put x into THAT one.\n\n- Both wirings give the correct answer. Only the speed changes.\n\n- Our matrices are row major, so x goes into col (the usual convention).\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
